.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt SPACECENTRICITY 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm spacecentricity
.Nd Spacecentricity project utilities and QMK firmware development
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a maximalist QMK firmware implementation. This document contains an
overview of the collection of POSIX-compliant shell utilities for
maintaining the project and its integration with QMK.
.Pp
The project utilities are located in the
.Pa scripts/
directory. Together they provide a small command suite for installing
and removing the keymap, installing project documentation, maintaining
license headers, and building and testing the firmware.
.Pp
Each utility is independently documented in its own manual page.
.Sh UTILITIES
.Bl -tag -width "license_headers.sh"
.It Xr install.sh 1
Create a symbolic link from the QMK keymap directory to the
Spacecentricity keymap.
.It Xr uninstall.sh 1
Remove the Spacecentricity keymap symlink and any project manual pages
installed by
.Xr install_man.sh 1 .
.It Xr install_man.sh 1
Install or remove the project's manual pages.
.It Xr license_headers.sh 1
Add or remove copyright and license headers from project source files.
.It Xr build.sh 1
Build, flash, lint, clean, check status, or open the QMK debug console
for the Spacecentricity keymap.
.El
.Sh QMK INTEGRATION
The project targets the
.Qq inland/mk47
keyboard and integrates with a local QMK firmware checkout.
.Pp
By default, the QMK checkout is expected to be at
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
This location may be overridden with the
.Ev QMK_PATH
environment variable.
.Pp
The Spacecentricity keymap is exposed to QMK through a symbolic link
rather than by copying project files into the QMK source tree. This
allows the working copy to remain in the project repository while QMK
operates on it from its expected keymap path.
.Sh WORKFLOW
A typical project workflow consists of:
.Bl -enum
.It
Run
.Xr install.sh 1
to link the keymap into the QMK checkout.
.It
Run
.Xr install_man.sh 1
to install the project manual pages.
.It
Use
.Xr build.sh 1
to build, lint, check, or flash the firmware.
.It
Use
.Xr license_headers.sh 1
when maintaining source-file license headers.
.It
Run
.Xr uninstall.sh 1
to remove the QMK integration and installed manual pages.
.It
Periodically update the QMK firmware checkout with
.Ic git pull
to keep the local QMK tree current.
.El
.Sh PROJECT ROOT
The project root provides convenience stubs for selected utilities.
In particular, the
.Pa build
stub invokes
.Xr build.sh 1
without requiring the script's path to be specified explicitly.
.Pp
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./build
\&./build -f
\&./build --check
.Ed
.Sh DOCUMENTATION
The project manual pages are maintained in
.Pa docs/man/
using the
.Xr mdoc 7
format.
.Pp
The manual pages may be installed with
.Xr install_man.sh 1
and removed as part of
.Xr uninstall.sh 1 .
.Pp
The installed pages provide detailed command reference for each project
utility, while
.Nm
serves as an overview of how the utilities relate to one another.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "scripts/license_headers.sh"
.It Pa scripts/
Project shell utilities.
.It Pa docs/man/
Project manual pages in
.Xr mdoc 7
source format.
.It Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware
Default QMK firmware checkout.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
